@startuml sequence01
autonumber

title Sequence View - Level 1\nSubmit Vessel Visit Notification (High-Level Flow)

actor "Shipping Agent\nRepresentative" as SAR
participant "Frontend" as SPA
participant "IAM Provider" as IAM
participant "Backend API" as API
participant "Database" as DB

== Authentication ==
SAR -> SPA: Access system
SPA -> IAM: Authenticate user
IAM -> IAM: Verify credentials
IAM --> SPA: Return access token
SPA -> API: Validate token & get role
API --> SPA: Return user role & permissions
SPA -> SPA: Render appropriate UI

== Submit Vessel Visit Notification ==
SAR -> SPA: Fill visit notification form\n(vessel, ETA/ETD, cargo manifest)
SPA -> SPA: Validate form data\n(ISO 6346 container IDs)

SAR -> SPA: Submit notification
SPA -> API: POST /api/vesselvisitnotifications\n(Authorization: Bearer token)
API -> API: Validate user authorization
API -> API: Validate business rules
API -> DB: Check vessel exists
DB --> API: Vessel data
API -> DB: Check agent authorized for vessel
DB --> API: Authorization confirmed
API -> DB: Save notification (status: "submitted")
DB --> API: Notification created
API --> SPA: 201 Created (notification DTO)
SPA --> SAR: Display success message

== View Notification Status ==
SAR -> SPA: View my notifications
SPA -> API: GET /api/vesselvisitnotifications\n?representativeId=xxx
API -> DB: Query notifications
DB --> API: Notification list
API --> SPA: Return notification DTOs
SPA --> SAR: Display notifications with status

note right of API
  Status can be:
  - In Progress
  - Submitted
  - Pending Approval
  - Approved
  - Rejected
end note

@enduml